{{Classic Era}}
'''The skill that governs the use of bow-type ranged weapons.''' Archery provides [[Warrior]]s and [[Rogue]]s with a ranged attack skill to safely pull enemies, gives [[Shadow Knight]]s and [[Paladin]]s a long-range attack that does not use mana, and is especially useful to [[Ranger]]s for kiting, pulling, and ranged DPS.

== Classes ==

*[[Ranger]] (Max 270)
*[[Warrior]] (Max 240)
*[[Rogue]] (Max 240)
*[[Shadow Knight]] (Max 75)
*[[Paladin]] (Max 75)

== Archery and Stats ==

ATK affects archery the same way it affects melee. Higher Archery ATK compared to the target's Mitigation AC improves the chance of landing hits closer to maximum damage, increasing average damage per hit.

Archery also uses Dexterity. The ATK number shown in the inventory is main-hand melee ATK and does not represent offhand or archery ATK. Archery uses its own skill and Dexterity-based attack value.

Archery ATK is not currently shown on the character sheet, but items, AAs, and buffs that increase ATK also affect archery.

