Across all five rounds, the quiver setups averaged approximately 20% more bow attacks than the no-quiver setup, matching the listed haste of [[Fleeting Quiver]]. The lower matching-arrow results are normal test variance caused by combat-log timing and uneven attack entries, not evidence of a different haste value.

Overall, the testing supports approximately 20% bow haste from the quiver, whether it contains a matching arrow, a mismatched arrow, or no arrow at all.

== Damage Calculation ==

Archery damage is based on the bow and the arrow being fired.

A bow with 10 damage, 40 delay, and 100 range combined with an arrow with 5 damage and 50 range functions as a weapon with:

*15 damage.
*40 delay.
*150 range.

The arrow fired from the bow affects damage and range. The arrow stored inside the quiver does not affect quiver haste or the damage of the shot.

== Range ==

Archery range does not cap at 300.

Testing confirmed that a 200-range bow combined with 150-range arrows has a total range of 350. Larger hitboxes increase the distance from which a target can be shot, and Z-axis distance also affects archery range.

This is useful against [[Dragon_Roar]], which has a PBAoE range of 300. A player can potentially stand outside fear range and continue dealing ranged damage with careful positioning.

== Trueshot and Ranger DPS ==

'''Trueshot is not currently part of EQ Legends.'''

Rangers can deal respectable DPS with a good bow and the [[Trueshot Discipline]]. This is especially useful when area effects, poor hitboxes, or other mechanics make it difficult for melee characters to stay engaged.

Rangers receive innate double damage against non-rooted, stationary mobs starting at level 51. This helps offset the fact that archery does not double attack power in the same way as melee.

A Ranger using an [[Exquisite Velium Reinforced Bow]] and [[Mithril Champion Arrows]] is effectively using the equivalent of a 38/36 two-handed weapon with 340 range, without damage bonus or double attack.

[[Trueshot Discipline]] slightly more than doubles Ranger bow damage for two minutes. With Trueshot active, the result is approximately equivalent to a 38/36 two-handed weapon that always double attacks, can critically hit, and does not have a damage bonus.

